      "id": "cet4-paper-2021123-part-3",
      "title": "Part III                              Reading Comprehension                                      (40 minutes)",
      "layout": "flow",
      "instructions": [],
      "groups": [
        {
          "id": "cet4-paper-2021123-part-3-section-2-group-1",
          "title": "题目",
          "presentation": "reading",
          "instructions": [],
          "stimulusBlocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Each statement contains information given in one of the paragraphs. Identify the paragraph"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "from which the information is derived. You may choose a paragraph more than once. Each"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "paragraph is marked with a letter. Answer the questions by marking the corresponding letter on"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Answer Sheet 2."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Why it matters that teens are reading less"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "A) Most of us spend much more time with digital media than we did a decade ago. But"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "today's teens have grown up with smartphones. Compared with teens a couple of"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "decades ago, the way they interact with traditional media like books and movies is"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "fundamentally different."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "B) Analysis of surveys of over one million teens in the United States collected since 1976"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "reveals a major shift in how teens are spending their leisure time. Paper books are being"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "ignored, in favor of screens. Digital devices are changing other behaviors, too. More"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "and more, young people choose spending time on their electronic devices over engaging"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "in other activities, regardless of the type. Indeed, by 2016, the average American high"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "school senior said they spent six hours a day writing text messages, on social media,"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "and online during their free time. And that covers just three activities, and if other"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "digital media activities were included, that estimate would no doubt rise."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "C) Teens did not always spend that much time with digital media. Online time has doubled"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "since 2006, and social media use has moved from a periodic activity to a daily one in the"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "same period. By 2016, nearly nine out of ten young women in the 12th grade said they"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "visited social media sites every day. Meanwhile, time spent playing video games rose"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "from under an hour a day to an hour and a half on average. One out of ten American 8th"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "grade students in 201 6 spent 40 hours a week or more playing video games. Let me"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "emphasize that this is equal to the time most adults spend per week at work."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "D) If teens are spending so much time using electronic devices, does that mean they have"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "to give up some other activities? Maybe not. Over the years, many scholars have"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
